# Code Blue Navi — Installation Guide
### UCI Health ALERT Team

---

## What is it?
Code Blue Navi is a resuscitation timing and documentation tool designed specifically for our team. It runs on your phone like an app but installs directly from your browser — no App Store required.

---

## iPhone Instructions

> ⚠️ **You must use Safari.** It will not work correctly from Chrome or other browsers on iPhone.

**Step 1** — Open Safari and go to:
```
[YOUR GITHUB PAGES URL HERE]
```

**Step 2** — Tap the **Share button** at the bottom of the screen
*(the box with an arrow pointing up)*

**Step 3** — Scroll down and tap **"Add to Home Screen"**

**Step 4** — The name should say **Code Blue Navi** — tap **Add** in the top right

**Step 5** — Go to your home screen and find the Code Blue Navi icon

**Step 6** — Before your first use, tap the icon to open it, then tap **START CODE** once to unlock audio, then tap **Reset All** to clear it. This activates the sound alerts.

✅ The app will now work **without internet** after this first load.

---

## Android Instructions

**Step 1** — Open **Chrome** and go to:
```
[YOUR GITHUB PAGES URL HERE]
```

**Step 2** — Tap the **three-dot menu** in the top right corner

**Step 3** — Tap **"Add to Home Screen"** or **"Install App"**
*(wording varies by phone model)*

**Step 4** — Tap **Add**

**Step 5** — Find the Code Blue Navi icon in your app drawer or home screen

**Step 6** — Open it once with internet to fully load, then it works offline.

✅ The app will now work **without internet** after this first load.

